; The compression table. Nobody writes one of these: the 1991 compiler
; is single pass, so it cannot pick the tokens itself -- that would take
; reading every text first to count what repeats. Authors included a
; table shipped with DAAD, one per language, or produced their own with
; the FINDTOK utility from a scan file the compiler wrote with -t.
;
; It is reproduced here byte for byte so that recompiling yields the
; same database: a different table compresses the texts differently.
; Editing it changes every text that refers to it.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Every text may refer to these, so the section comes before any text.
; Spaces are written as the null word character.
; The first entry is a placeholder no text refers to: every interpreter
; skips it, but it has to be there and be one byte long.

